===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|legal}} A [[formal]] [[question]] or set of questions [[submitted]] to [[opposing]] [[party]] to [[answer]], generally [[governed]] by [[court]] rule.
#* {{RQ:Catharine Macaulay History of England|passage=Sidney interposed with an '''interrogatory''' concerning the legality of the evidence}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=11 Dec 76|volume=4|number=24|journal=Gay Community News|page=3|title=Security Clearance Cleared|text=Kimberling, on the advice of his lawyer Frank Kameny, refused to answer several questions put to him on the 16-question '''interrogatory'''. After strong objections, the questions in question were withdrawn.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2013|author=James J. Gross|title=It's Splitsville: Surviving Your Divorce|page=240
|passage=If those attempts are unsuccessful, the attorney requesting the '''interrogatories''' may file a motion for sanctions with the court. The sanctions range from attorney fees to prohibiting the nonanswering party from presenting or defending claims.}}
# A [[question]]; an [[interrogation]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1798|author=Eleanor Sleath|title=The Orphan of the Rhine
|passage=But when he found that some of his '''interrogatories''' were evaded, and others answered undecisively, the look of gentleness which he had assumed, vanished, and his brow wore the cloud of disappointment and of anger.}}

